{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And all these things, etc.</b> Now the meaning is otherwise: for it is in my dominion and mine, for this throne and footstool — I made them." "<b>And all these things shall be.</b> Joined to <b>my hand made</b>." "<b>To this one I will look.</b> The meaning: even though the heavens are my throne, I will look to the poor and broken-spirited. The meaning of אביט is \"I will set my eyes upon him.\" Now it is the opposite of <b>I will hide my eyes from you</b> (Isaiah 1:15)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 66, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:09.661468247Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}